From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:17:32 -0400
Subject: spaces: one sidebar for every window, the SpaceRegistry

A profile-level SpaceRegistry (a KeyedService, kept in the preference
stedding.spaces.registry) owns the Space list: order, names, icons,
colours, and a profile id that stays empty in round 6. Every normal
window's SpaceModel mirrors it: the first window of a profile seeds the
registry with the Spaces its session brought, later windows merge theirs
and then follow the registry whole, and every mutator (add, remove, move,
rename, icon, colour) goes through the registry and comes back to every
window through its observer. The window keeps only its active Space and
its tabs' memberships, so the session's per-window data and the rebuild
path stay as they were. A Blank Window (opt-shift-cmd-N, the bar) opts out
with one Space of its own; a private window has no model at all
(docs/features/windows.md G0-G1, G3-G5; ADR 0016).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 4, R6-31: cmd-N must show the same sidebar.
Removable when: Chromium's tab strip keeps workspaces per profile.
